    "result_text": "The full build passes. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Change: `salutation` derived from optional `title`\n\nThe request may now include a `title` (e.g. MR/MRS/MS/DR); the owner response exposes `salutation` = `title + \" \" + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is given.\n\n### Files changed\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 the API contract (DTOs are code-generated from it):\n   - Added `title` as an optional editable field on `OwnerFields` (the request body).\n   - Added `salutation` as a read-only derived field on `Owner` (the response), alongside the existing derived fields like `displayName`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`**:\n   - Added the persisted `title` column with getter/setter.\n   - Added `getSalutation()`, a derived getter that composes `title + \" \" + lastName`, falling back to just the last name when the title is null/empty. This sits next to the other owner-derived getters, keeping the logic where it belongs rather than in the controller.\n\n3. **DB schemas** (`db/hsqldb`, `db/h2`, `db/postgres`, `db/mysql` `schema.sql`) \u2014 added the `title` column to the `owners` table so the value survives the save-and-reload the test exercises (the test profile uses `ddl-auto=none` with the hsqldb schema).\n\n4. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.updateOwner`** \u2014 copies `title` through on update, consistent with the other editable fields.\n\nNo mapper changes were needed: MapStruct maps `title` (request\u2192entity) and `salutation` (entity\u2192response) automatically by name, exactly as it does for the other derived getters.\n\n### Design notes\n- I kept `title` a plain `String` rather than an OpenAPI `enum`. An enum would have generated a typed `TitleEnum` DTO getter, creating avoidable `enum`\u2194`String` conversion friction in both the mapper and the manual `updateOwner` copy, for validation the spec/tests don't require. The allowed values are documented in the field description instead.\n- `getSalutation()` lives on the model as a small single-responsibility derived accessor, mirroring the existing pattern (`getDisplayName`, `getMembershipNumber`, etc.).\n\n### Tests\n`./mvnw -o test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` (the new `coreComposesSalutation` acceptance test and the full suite pass).",
